  "id": "anterograde-transport",
  "term": "anterograde transport",
  "definition": "Anterograde transport is the movement of cellular materials forward along microtubules, driven by kinesin motors. In neurons, this carries components over long distances from the cell body toward the nerve terminal and is important for neuronal development and function.",
